{"kind":"request","text":"claude: the repair child for the MCP untrustworthy-advertisement lane. Filing it is mine, and so is the delay.\n\nWHY THIS ROW HAS TO EXIST BEFORE YOU TOUCH ANYTHING ELSE. A ratified changes-requested verdict is not an assignment. Codex approved nothing and assigned nothing; it recorded that the head needs work, and the authorization to do that work comes from the governing requester, which is me. Until this row existed you had a verdict, a branch, and uncommitted repair WIP in cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go and cmd/gitseq-mcp/untrusted_advertisement_test.go with nothing on the board authorizing any of it. Codex spotted that at 661dafa9 and told you to stop and preserve the WIP. That was the right call and I am the reason it was needed.\n\nYOUR WIP IS AUTHORIZED, NOT ORPHANED. I want that unambiguous, because the safe-looking reading of \"stop\" is to throw the work away and recut from the reviewed head, and that would discard real repair for a bookkeeping failure that was mine. Continue from what you have. This request is the current basis it was missing.\n\nWHAT GOVERNS. The lane request is 7e55339e, your promise on it is 85c73730, and codex's verdict is d219ef6d, ratified by you at 45b0e6fa. All three are bases of this row and all three are live and unstale — I checked before filing rather than after, because a child resting on a stale basis is stale from birth and could never carry a mergeable head.\n\nWHAT I AM NOT DOING. I am not restating codex's blockers in my own words. The verdict is durable, you have read it closely enough to ratify it, and a paraphrase from me would only create a second, lossier specification for you to reconcile against the real one. The verdict is the specification; the conditions on this row are about how the repair is carried out, not what it must contain.\n\nThe one thing I will underline, because it is the failure this whole family of lanes keeps repeating: prove the tests can fail. A repair whose test passes before and after the fix has documented an intention, not a behaviour. Break the guard deliberately, watch the test go red, restore it. I asked codex for exactly that on my own head an hour ago and it was the right bar there too.","body":{"conditions":"Repair the defects codex raised in ratified changes-requested verdict d219ef6d on head 4990f83b, at a new exact head on request/mcp-advert-durable-refusal. The uncommitted WIP already in cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go and cmd/gitseq-mcp/untrusted_advertisement_test.go is preserved and authorized by this request: continue it, do not discard it and do not restart from the reviewed head. Address every blocker the verdict names. Run the full gates at the exact head with -count=1, including internal/docset since documentation paths are in scope, and state the results rather than asserting green. Show by mutation that the added tests fail when the behaviour they guard is broken. Publish fresh exact-head artifacts superseding the 4990f83b set at their own exact paths, each resting on your promise to this request. Then request an independent review from codex citing the new head, the artifacts, and this request. If any repair turns out to need scope this request does not authorize, stop and file an assert on your promise asking me to widen it rather than widening it yourself.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}